      "classification": "editorial-candidate",
      "rationale": "The example computes the nine vertices of B(lambda_1) tensor B(lambda_1), identifies its two highest vertices, and explicitly enumerates the colored arrows in each component. A graph would make the six-vertex B(2 lambda_1) component and three-vertex B(lambda_2) component immediately visible.",
      "labels_maps_relations_to_draw_or_check": "Draw all vertices (j,k)=u_j tensor u_k for 1<=j,k<=3, with arrows labeled 1 or 2. Component one: (1,1)-1->(2,1)-1->(2,2); (2,1)-2->(3,1)-1->(3,2); (2,2)-2->(3,2)-2->(3,3). Component two: (1,2)-2->(1,3)-1->(2,3). Mark highest vertices (1,1) of weight 2 lambda_1 and (1,2) of weight lambda_2. Check that all nine vertices occur exactly once and that raising arrows reverse the displayed lowering arrows. The graph is explanatory; the proof remains the source of the enumeration.",
